1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,013
From your very first paycheck,

2
00:00:02,013 --> 00:00:05,769
modern culture hands you a remarkably narrow scoreboard:

3
00:00:05,769 --> 00:00:08,453
one single number inside a bank account.

4
00:00:08,453 --> 00:00:13,015
That single-metric obsession explains one of the strangest paradoxes

5
00:00:13,015 --> 00:00:16,034
of modern success - how someone can hit seven

6
00:00:16,034 --> 00:00:18,650
figures on paper yet wake up exhausted,

7
00:00:18,650 --> 00:00:19,254
isolated,

8
00:00:19,254 --> 00:00:22,407
and chained to a calendar they secretly resent.

9
00:00:22,407 --> 00:00:25,560
As writer Sahil Bloom highlights in The 5 Types

10
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:26,231
of Wealth,

11
00:00:26,231 --> 00:00:30,524
a genuinely rich life actually runs on five distinct currencies:

12
00:00:30,524 --> 00:00:31,329
Time Wealth,

13
00:00:31,329 --> 00:00:32,269
Social Wealth,

14
00:00:32,269 --> 00:00:33,208
Mental Wealth,

15
00:00:33,208 --> 00:00:34,281
Physical Wealth,

16
00:00:34,281 --> 00:00:35,690
and Financial Wealth.

17
00:00:35,690 --> 00:00:38,426
Start with Time Wealth and Social Wealth.

18
00:00:38,426 --> 00:00:41,697
Time Wealth is not merely retiring at sixty-five;

19
00:00:41,697 --> 00:00:44,566
it is daily autonomy over what you work on,

20
00:00:44,566 --> 00:00:45,501
where you sit,

21
00:00:45,501 --> 00:00:47,436
and whom you build alongside.

22
00:00:47,436 --> 00:00:49,438
Time data makes this sobering:

23
00:00:49,438 --> 00:00:53,510
roughly ninety percent of total in-person hours with children

24
00:00:53,510 --> 00:00:55,712
happen before they turn eighteen,

25
00:00:55,712 --> 00:00:59,650
and visits with aging parents are often measured in dozens,

26
00:00:59,650 --> 00:01:00,451
not decades.

27
00:01:00,451 --> 00:01:01,118
Meanwhile,

28
00:01:01,118 --> 00:01:05,723
the eighty-five-year Harvard Study of Adult Development proved Social

29
00:01:05,723 --> 00:01:09,327
Wealth is biological armor - relationship depth at age

30
00:01:09,327 --> 00:01:13,398
fifty predicted health and satisfaction at eighty better than

31
00:01:13,398 --> 00:01:13,732
fame,

32
00:01:13,732 --> 00:01:13,999
IQ,

33
00:01:13,999 --> 00:01:15,000
or cholesterol.

34
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:18,064
Next come Mental Wealth and Physical Wealth.

35
00:01:18,064 --> 00:01:20,361
Mental Wealth combines curiosity,

36
00:01:20,361 --> 00:01:20,918
purpose,

37
00:01:20,918 --> 00:01:23,843
and inner peace - the rare capacity to sit

38
00:01:23,843 --> 00:01:27,463
in a silent room for thirty minutes without drowning

39
00:01:27,463 --> 00:01:31,014
in status anxiety or reaching for a glowing screen.

40
00:01:31,014 --> 00:01:33,382
Physical Wealth is daily vitality,

41
00:01:33,382 --> 00:01:34,635
restorative sleep,

42
00:01:34,635 --> 00:01:35,262
strength,

43
00:01:35,262 --> 00:01:37,211
and mobility across decades.

44
00:01:37,211 --> 00:01:40,693
Think of Physical and Mental Wealth as the leading

45
00:01:40,693 --> 00:01:44,383
digit 'one' standing in front of every financial zero

46
00:01:44,383 --> 00:01:45,427
you accumulate.

47
00:01:45,427 --> 00:01:48,491
Stack six zeros behind a healthy one and you

48
00:01:48,491 --> 00:01:49,535
hold a million;

49
00:01:49,535 --> 00:01:52,808
erase that leading one and every zero behind it

50
00:01:52,808 --> 00:01:54,270
collapses to nothing.

51
00:01:54,270 --> 00:01:55,461
Here is where smart,

52
00:01:55,461 --> 00:01:57,427
hard-working people get ambushed.

53
00:01:57,427 --> 00:01:59,512
Between ages twenty-five and fifty,

54
00:01:59,512 --> 00:02:03,385
millions play what psychologists call the Deferred Life Strategy:

55
00:02:03,385 --> 00:02:05,172
aggressively liquidating Time,

56
00:02:05,172 --> 00:02:05,589
Social,

57
00:02:05,589 --> 00:02:06,006
Mental,

58
00:02:06,006 --> 00:02:08,985
and Physical wealth to stockpile Financial wealth,

59
00:02:08,985 --> 00:02:12,559
assuming they can simply repurchase the first four at sixty.

60
00:02:12,559 --> 00:02:13,393
Unfortunately,

61
00:02:13,393 --> 00:02:16,133
compound interest works in reverse on neglect.

62
00:02:16,133 --> 00:02:18,457
Neglected friendships quietly dissolve,

63
00:02:18,457 --> 00:02:20,720
missed childhood summers never replay,

64
00:02:20,720 --> 00:02:23,937
and twenty years of chronic stress and five-hour sleep

65
00:02:23,937 --> 00:02:27,750
nights carry biological interest rates money can rarely reverse.

66
00:02:27,750 --> 00:02:30,925
Financial Wealth only shines when it serves as a

67
00:02:30,925 --> 00:02:34,695
freedom engine rather than an infinite status tournament.

68
00:02:34,695 --> 00:02:38,796
Author Kurt Vonnegut once teased fellow novelist Joseph Heller

69
00:02:38,796 --> 00:02:41,508
at a billionaire hedge-fund host's party,

70
00:02:41,508 --> 00:02:44,484
pointing out that their host earned more in a

71
00:02:44,484 --> 00:02:48,254
single day than Heller's classic novel Catch-22 earned in

72
00:02:48,254 --> 00:02:48,783
history.

73
00:02:48,783 --> 00:02:52,024
Heller smiled and replied that he owned one thing

74
00:02:52,024 --> 00:02:53,876
the billionaire never would:

75
00:02:53,876 --> 00:02:56,059
the knowledge that he had enough.

76
00:02:56,059 --> 00:02:58,638
Without a written definition of enough,

77
00:02:58,638 --> 00:03:02,210
every income jump simply pushes the goalpost ten yards

78
00:03:02,210 --> 00:03:03,070
further away.

79
00:03:03,070 --> 00:03:06,513
Put this framework into practice this Sunday with a

80
00:03:06,513 --> 00:03:08,674
ten-minute Life Portfolio Audit.

81
00:03:08,674 --> 00:03:09,079
First,

82
00:03:09,079 --> 00:03:11,104
score all five buckets - Time,

83
00:03:11,104 --> 00:03:11,577
Social,

84
00:03:11,577 --> 00:03:12,049
Mental,

85
00:03:12,049 --> 00:03:12,657
Physical,

86
00:03:12,657 --> 00:03:15,425
and Financial - honestly from one to ten.

87
00:03:15,425 --> 00:03:15,898
Second,

88
00:03:15,898 --> 00:03:18,801
write one strict Anti-Goal for each pillar:

89
00:03:18,801 --> 00:03:23,257
non-negotiable boundaries you refuse to cross during busy seasons,

90
00:03:23,257 --> 00:03:26,430
such as never missing three family dinners in a

91
00:03:26,430 --> 00:03:29,940
row or never trading a morning walk for low-priority

92
00:03:29,940 --> 00:03:30,345
email.

93
00:03:30,345 --> 00:03:30,886
Finally,

94
00:03:30,886 --> 00:03:35,139
put one concrete thirty-minute deposit on Monday's calendar for

95
00:03:35,139 --> 00:03:37,232
whichever pillar scored lowest,

96
00:03:37,232 --> 00:03:40,810
so your life rebalances long before crisis forces it.
